        # List where silent verification runs
        #
        # Where silent verification runs: every country where at least one mobile network can run the check, and per
        # country the networks that can. Read this instead of hardcoding a list, because coverage grows as networks
        # approve the feature.
        #
        # `approval` says whether a network answers for production traffic (`live`) or only while it approves
        # production use (`test`), in which case it answers for the verified test numbers of a registration. `wifi`
        # says whether the SIM check also runs over Wi-Fi, so a device without mobile data can still complete it.
        #
        # **Narrowing.** `country` answers for one ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country.
        #
        # **Before you start.** `POST /v3/phone/silent/eligibility/` answers for one number, and a silent check that
        # cannot run falls back to the verification's code channels.
        #
        # **Authentication.** Send your application's API key in `x-api-key`.
        #
        # **Rate limit.** Requests count against the key's budget; over it the answer is `429` with `Retry-After`.
        #
        # +GET /v3/phone/silent/coverage/+
        #
        # @param country [String] Only this ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country.
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneSilentCoverage]
        def coverage(country: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :get,
            "/v3/phone/silent/coverage/",
            query: {
              "country" => country
            },
            response: Types::PhoneSilentCoverage,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # Check silent eligibility before you start
        #
        # Whether a silent check can run for one number now, so you can decide whether to offer it before you start a
        # verification. `eligible` is the answer and, when it is `false`, `reason` says why: `unsupported_network`
        # (the number's mobile network cannot run the check), `not_mobile_data` (the device is not on mobile data) or
        # `country_not_covered` (silent verification does not run in the number's country).
        #
        # `network` is the mobile network the number belongs to, `country` its ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code, and
        # `wifi_possible` whether the SIM check can still run over Wi-Fi when the device has no mobile data.
        #
        # **Mobile data.** Send `ip_address`, the phone's public IP, to have the answer also confirm the device is on
        # mobile data. Without it, the answer is about the network alone.
        #
        # **What follows.** A verification that runs the silent check first falls back to its next code channel when
        # the check cannot run.
        #
        # **Authentication.** Send your application's API key in `x-api-key`. To check a client SDK's publishable key
        # as well, include it in `X-Publishable-Key`.
        #
        # **Rate limit.** Requests count against the key's budget; over it the answer is `429` with `Retry-After`.
        #
        # +POST /v3/phone/silent/eligibility/+
        #
        # @param phone_number [String] The number in international format (E.164), for example `+34600000012`.
        # @param ip_address [String] The phone's public IP, so the answer also confirms the device is on mobile data.
        # @param idempotency_key [String] sent as the Idempotency-Key header
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneSilentEligibility]
        def eligibility(phone_number:, ip_address: OMIT, idempotency_key: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :post,
            "/v3/phone/silent/eligibility/",
            body: {
              "phone_number" => phone_number,
              "ip_address" => ip_address
            },
            headers: { "Idempotency-Key" => idempotency_key },
            response: Types::PhoneSilentEligibility,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # The +phone.silent.registrations+ resource.
        class Registrations < Didit::Resource
          # Submit a country for carrier approval of silent verification
          #
          # Submit a country for carrier approval of silent verification, so silent checks run for your application's
          # production traffic there: `country`, the `use_case` it runs in, your `company_name` and the `website`
          # where the flow runs. Optionally name the `networks` to ask, your expected `monthly_volume` and links to
          # `flow_screenshots`.
          #
          # The answer is the registration. `status` starts `submitted`, moves to `in_review`, and ends as `approved`,
          # `partly_approved` (some networks approved and some rejected) or `rejected`. `networks` lists each mobile
          # network's own decision and `live_at` is when silent verification went live for you in the country.
          #
          # **One per country.** A country with an open registration answers `409 registration_exists`: track that one
          # with `GET /v3/phone/silent/registrations/{registration_id}/` instead.
          #
          # **Authentication.** Send your application's API key in `x-api-key`.
          #
          # **Rate limit.** Requests count against the key's budget; over it the answer is `429` with `Retry-After`.
          #
          # +POST /v3/phone/silent/registrations/+
          #
          # @param country [String] The ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country to ask approval for.
          # @param use_case [String] What silent verification is used for.
          # @param company_name [String] Your legal company name, as the networks see it.
          # @param website [String] Where the flow runs, so the networks can review it.
          # @param networks [Array<String>] The mobile networks to ask, by the names `GET /v3/phone/silent/coverage/`
          #   lists; all the country's networks when you send none
          # @param monthly_volume [Integer, nil] Expected silent checks a month.
          # @param flow_screenshots [Array<String>] Links to screens of the flow, as the networks ask for them.
          # @param idempotency_key [String] sent as the Idempotency-Key header
          # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
          # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneSilentRegistration]
          def create(
            country:,
            use_case:,
            company_name:,
            website:,
            networks: OMIT,
            monthly_volume: OMIT,
            flow_screenshots: OMIT,
            idempotency_key: OMIT,
            request_options: nil
          )
            @client.request(
              :post,
              "/v3/phone/silent/registrations/",
              body: {
                "country" => country,
                "use_case" => use_case,
                "company_name" => company_name,
                "website" => website,
                "networks" => networks,
                "monthly_volume" => monthly_volume,
                "flow_screenshots" => flow_screenshots
              },
              headers: { "Idempotency-Key" => idempotency_key },
              response: Types::PhoneSilentRegistration,
              request_options: request_options
            )
          end

          # Track a carrier approval, network by network
          #
          # Track a carrier approval, network by network: the registration's `status`, each mobile network's decision
          # (`status`, `decided_at` and, when it rejected the request, `reason`), and `live_at` once silent
          # verification is live for you in the country.
          #
          # A registration that is `partly_approved` runs silent verification on the networks that approved it.
          #
          # **Authentication.** Send your application's API key in `x-api-key`.
          #
          # **Rate limit.** Requests count against the key's budget; over it the answer is `429` with `Retry-After`.
          #
          # +GET /v3/phone/silent/registrations/{registration_id}/+
          #
          # @param registration_id [String] The registration id, `sr_` followed by 32 hexadecimal characters (an `nr_`
          #   id of a silent verification registration works too).
          # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
          # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneSilentRegistration]
          def retrieve(registration_id, request_options: nil)
            @client.request(
              :get,
              "/v3/phone/silent/registrations/{registration_id}/",
              path_params: { "registration_id" => registration_id },
              response: Types::PhoneSilentRegistration,
              request_options: request_options
            )
          end
        end
      end

      # The +phone.stats+ resource.
      class Stats < Didit::Resource
        # Conversion, delivery time and spend, grouped
        #
        # Read conversion, delivery times and spend in USD for the requested product and date range. Each entry in
        # `rows` identifies its group in `key`. Choose a grouping supported by that product in `group_by`.
        #
        # For `verification`, read and reply rates are always `0`. For `messages`, silent success and code-free share
        # are always `0`. For `lookups`, only spend applies, so all rates and delivery percentiles are `0`. A rate or
        # percentile a group has no events for is `0`, never `null`.
        #
        # **Errors.** `400 invalid_product`: not a product this endpoint groups. `400 invalid_group`: not a grouping
        # this product supports. `400 stats_window_too_wide`: the range is longer than a year. `400` naming `to`: `to`
        # is a date no window can end on, such as `9999-12-31`, the last date there is; the body is `{"to": ["to must
        # be a date a window can end on, before 9999-12-31."]}`.
        #
        # A scoped API key needs `phone: read`.
        #
        # +GET /v3/phone/stats/+
        #
        # @param product [String] The product to report on.
        # @param group_by [String] For `verification`, use `country`, `channel`, `network`, `line_type` or `day`. For
        #   `messages`, use `country`, `channel` or `day`. For `lookups`, use `country`, `network`, `line_type` or
        #   `day`. Defaults to `day`.
        # @param from [Date, String] The first day, as YYYY-MM-DD.
        # @param to [Date, String] The last day, as YYYY-MM-DD, before `9999-12-31`.
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneStatsResponse]
        def retrieve(product: OMIT, group_by: OMIT, from: OMIT, to: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :get,
            "/v3/phone/stats/",
            query: {
              "product" => product,
              "group_by" => group_by,
              "from" => from,
              "to" => to
            },
            response: Types::PhoneStatsResponse,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end
      end

      # The +phone.verifications+ resource.
      class Verifications < Didit::Resource
        # Mark a verification verified
        #
        # Mark a verification verified after your own code check. It counts in Verifications, Analytics and the events
        # like any other verification, and `verified_by` is `api`. `reason` defaults to `own_code_check`. A
        # verification that already ended returns `409 already_final`. Only verifications your application started
        # with `POST /v3/phone/send/` can be changed here: a Phone step of a hosted verification session is read-only
        # and returns `404 not_found`.
        #
        # +POST /v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/approve/+
        #
        # @param verification_id [String] The verification.
        # @param reason [String] own_code_check (default): your backend checked the code it sent with code.
        # @param idempotency_key [String] sent as the Idempotency-Key header
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneVerificationApproveResponse]
        def approve(verification_id, reason: OMIT, idempotency_key: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :post,
            "/v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/approve/",
            path_params: { "verification_id" => verification_id },
            body: {
              "reason" => reason
            },
            headers: { "Idempotency-Key" => idempotency_key },
            response: Types::PhoneVerificationApproveResponse,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # Cancel a verification
        #
        # Cancel a verification. The code stops working and unsent steps are not charged. If the code window elapsed
        # but the verification has yet to be finalized, cancellation returns `200` with status `cancelled` even if the
        # verification history shows `expired`. A verification already finalized as verified, blocked, cancelled or
        # expired returns `409 already_final`. Only verifications your application started with `POST /v3/phone/send/`
        # can be changed here: a Phone step of a hosted verification session is read-only and returns `404 not_found`.
        #
        # +POST /v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/cancel/+
        #
        # @param verification_id [String] The verification.
        # @param idempotency_key [String] sent as the Idempotency-Key header
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneVerificationCancelResponse]
        def cancel(verification_id, idempotency_key: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :post,
            "/v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/cancel/",
            path_params: { "verification_id" => verification_id },
            headers: { "Idempotency-Key" => idempotency_key },
            response: Types::PhoneVerificationCancelResponse,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # List or export verifications
        #
        # List your application's verifications, newest first. Filter by status, channel, phone number, reference, tag
        # (`key:value`) or creation time. Use `limit` and `offset` to page through JSON results: `next` and `previous`
        # are offsets, not URLs, so send `next` as `offset` to read the next page. Use `format=csv` to export all
        # matching verifications. The `template` query parameter does not filter these records. Verification history
        # does not return a `template_used` field.
        #
        # +GET /v3/phone/verifications/+
        #
        # @param status [String] pending, verified, not_delivered, expired, blocked or cancelled.
        # @param channel [String] Any channel.
        # @param phone_number [String] One number.
        # @param reference [String] Your reference.
        # @param tag [String] key:value, one of your tags.
        # @param created_after [Time, String] ISO 8601 date and time.
        # @param created_before [Time, String] ISO 8601 date and time.
        # @param limit [Integer] 20 by default, 100 at most.
        # @param offset [Integer] Where the page starts: 0 by default, or the `next` or `previous` value of another
        #   page.
        # @param format [String] json, or csv to export every row of the filtered list.
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Page<Didit::Types::PhoneVerificationDetail>]
        def list(
          status: OMIT,
          channel: OMIT,
          phone_number: OMIT,
          reference: OMIT,
          tag: OMIT,
          created_after: OMIT,
          created_before: OMIT,
          limit: OMIT,
          offset: OMIT,
          format: OMIT,
          request_options: nil
        )
          @client.request(
            :get,
            "/v3/phone/verifications/",
            query: {
              "status" => status,
              "channel" => channel,
              "phone_number" => phone_number,
              "reference" => reference,
              "tag" => tag,
              "created_after" => created_after,
              "created_before" => created_before,
              "limit" => limit,
              "offset" => offset,
              "format" => format
            },
            page: Types::PhoneVerificationDetail,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # Move to the next channel now
        #
        # Move to the next channel now, without waiting for the current step's timeout, or jump to `channel`. A
        # successful send keeps the same verification ID and expiry, but the new channel may deliver a different code
        # than the earlier sends; only [a same-window retry](/standalone-apis/phone-verifications-retry) promises the
        # same code. When every channel in the order was tried, the endpoint returns `409 no_next_channel`; a
        # verification that already ended returns `409 already_final`. Only verifications your application started
        # with `POST /v3/phone/send/` can be changed here: a Phone step of a hosted verification session is read-only
        # and returns `404 not_found`.
        #
        # +POST /v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/next/+
        #
        # @param verification_id [String] The verification.
        # @param channel [String] Jump to this channel instead of the next one.
        # @param idempotency_key [String] sent as the Idempotency-Key header
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneVerificationNextResponse]
        def next(verification_id, channel: OMIT, idempotency_key: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :post,
            "/v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/next/",
            path_params: { "verification_id" => verification_id },
            body: {
              "channel" => channel
            },
            headers: { "Idempotency-Key" => idempotency_key },
            response: Types::PhoneVerificationNextResponse,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # One verification with every attempt
        #
        # Retrieve one verification and its delivery attempts in order. Each attempt includes the channel, status,
        # network, route, delivery timestamps and price.
        #
        # +GET /v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/+
        #
        # @param verification_id [String] The verification.
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneVerificationDetail]
        def retrieve(verification_id, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :get,
            "/v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/",
            path_params: { "verification_id" => verification_id },
            response: Types::PhoneVerificationDetail,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end

        # Send the code again in the same window
        #
        # Resend the same code on its last delivery channel. The verification ID and expiry stay the same. Wait at
        # least 30 seconds after the last send. A verification allows up to three sends, including the first. To
        # change channels, use [the next-channel endpoint](/standalone-apis/phone-verifications-next). Only
        # verifications your application started with `POST /v3/phone/send/` can be changed here: a Phone step of a
        # hosted verification session is read-only and returns `404 not_found`.
        #
        # +POST /v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/retry/+
        #
        # @param verification_id [String] The verification.
        # @param channel [String] The last delivery channel. Requesting a different allowed channel returns `409
        #   code_not_resendable`.
        # @param idempotency_key [String] sent as the Idempotency-Key header
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneVerificationRetryResponse]
        def retry(verification_id, channel: OMIT, idempotency_key: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :post,
            "/v3/phone/verifications/{verification_id}/retry/",
            path_params: { "verification_id" => verification_id },
            body: {
              "channel" => channel
            },
            headers: { "Idempotency-Key" => idempotency_key },
            response: Types::PhoneVerificationRetryResponse,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end
      end

      # The +phone.voices+ resource.
      class Voices < Didit::Resource
        # List the voices that read codes aloud, per language
        #
        # List the voices that read verification codes aloud. Each locale has one default voice. Every voice includes
        # `sample_url`, which is currently `null` because no recordings are published. No operation takes a `voice_id`
        # yet.
        #
        # A scoped API key needs `phone: read`.
        #
        # +GET /v3/phone/voices/+
        #
        # @param locale [String] Filter by a canonical BCP 47 tag such as `es-ES` or `pt-BR`. A language alone returns
        #   every matching locale. For example, `pt` returns both `pt-BR` and `pt-PT`.
        # @param request_options [Hash, nil] :timeout, :max_retries, :extra_headers, :extra_query, :extra_body
        # @return [Didit::Types::PhoneVoiceListResponse]
        def list(locale: OMIT, request_options: nil)
          @client.request(
            :get,
            "/v3/phone/voices/",
            query: {
              "locale" => locale
            },
            response: Types::PhoneVoiceListResponse,
            request_options: request_options
          )
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
